id: procurement
name: Procurement and sourcing
industry: Supply chain & logistics
domain: Purchasing: suppliers, sourcing, contracts, purchase orders, receipts and supplier invoices
scope: Suppliers and their qualification, spend categories, purchase requisitions, sourcing events and bids, contracts, purchase orders, goods receipts, supplier invoices and three-way match, supplier performance.
summary: Describes how an organisation buys: who it buys from, what was requested and approved, which contract and order govern the purchase, what was received and what was invoiced. A starter model for procure-to-pay and spend analytics.
purpose: Shared vocabulary across e-procurement, ERP and accounts payable; basis for spend, compliance and supplier-performance analysis.
read: A Requisition raised by a Requester for a Cost centre leads to a Purchase order to a Supplier, optionally under a Contract awarded through a Sourcing event with Bids. Order lines name Items in a Spend category. Goods receipts confirm delivery; a Supplier invoice bills the order and is matched to order and receipt before Payment.
in: Suppliers; Requisition to order; Sourcing and contracts; Receipt, invoice, payment; Supplier performance
out: Inventory management; Production planning; General ledger; Logistics execution
std: ubl | high | Order, invoice and party structures follow OASIS UBL business documents. | Order, Invoice, Party, LineItem, PaymentMeans
std: unspsc | medium | Spend categories follow the UNSPSC hierarchy. | Segment, Family, Class, Commodity
std: schema | low | Organisations and invoices are aligned to schema.org. | schema:Organization, schema:Invoice
std: org | low | Cost centres map to organisational units. | org:OrganizationalUnit
== Supplier | Suppliers | Who we buy from.
Supplier | A company that sells goods or services to the organisation. | ~schema:Organization
  - supplier number : string !
  - name : string !
  - tax registration : string
  - country : string
  - onboarded on : date
  > has status > SupplierStatus 1
  > supplies category > SpendCategory *
SupplierStatus | Whether the supplier may be used.
  * Prospective, Approved, Preferred, Blocked
SupplierQualification | A check that a supplier meets a requirement, such as a certificate or audit.
  - requirement : string !
  - valid until : date
  - passed : boolean
  > of supplier > Supplier 1
SpendCategory | A class of goods or services bought; categories nest.
  - category code : string !
  - category name : string !
  > broader > SpendCategory ?
Item | A good or service that can be bought.
  - item code : string !
  - description : string !
  - unit : string
  > in category > SpendCategory 1
== Request | Requisition and order | Asking for and ordering things.
CostCentre | The organisational unit that bears the cost. | ~org:OrganizationalUnit
  - cost centre code : string !
  - name : string
Requester | A person who asks for a purchase.
  - employee number : string !
  - name : string
Requisition | An internal request to buy something, needing approval.
  - requisition number : string !
  - raised on : date !
  - estimated value : decimal
  - justification : string
  > raised by > Requester 1
  > charged to > CostCentre 1
  > has status > ApprovalStatus 1
ApprovalStatus | The approval state.
  * Draft, Pending approval, Approved, Rejected
PurchaseOrder | A binding order placed with a supplier.
  - po number : string !
  - ordered on : date !
  - total value : decimal
  - currency : string
  > placed with > Supplier 1 | | receives order
  > from requisition > Requisition ?
  > under contract > Contract ?
  > has status > PurchaseOrderStatus 1
PurchaseOrderLine | One item, quantity and price on a purchase order.
  - quantity : decimal !
  - unit price : decimal !
  - promised date : date
  > of order > PurchaseOrder 1 | | has line
  > for item > Item 1
PurchaseOrderStatus | The state of a purchase order.
  * Open, Partially received, Received, Closed, Cancelled
== Sourcing | Sourcing and contracts | Choosing suppliers and agreeing terms.
SourcingEvent | A request for quotation or tender inviting suppliers to bid.
  - event number : string !
  - opened on : date
  - closes on : date
  > for category > SpendCategory 1
Bid | A supplier's offer in a sourcing event.
  - bid amount : decimal !
  - submitted on : date
  - awarded : boolean
  > in event > SourcingEvent 1 | | has bid
  > by supplier > Supplier 1
Contract | An agreement with a supplier on prices and terms for a period.
  - contract number : string !
  - valid from : date !
  - valid to : date !
  - committed value : decimal
  - payment terms days : integer
  > with supplier > Supplier 1
  > awarded from > SourcingEvent ?
  > covers category > SpendCategory *
== Pay | Receipt, invoice and payment | Closing the loop.
GoodsReceipt | Confirmation that ordered goods or services were delivered.
  - receipt number : string !
  - received on : date !
  - quantity received : decimal !
  - quantity rejected : decimal
  > against line > PurchaseOrderLine 1
SupplierInvoice | A supplier's bill for goods or services. | ~schema:Invoice
  - invoice number : string !
  - invoice date : date !
  - amount : decimal !
  - due date : date
  > from supplier > Supplier 1
  > bills > PurchaseOrder ?
  > has match status > MatchStatus 1
MatchStatus | The result of comparing invoice, order and receipt.
  * Matched, Price variance, Quantity variance, No purchase order, On hold
SupplierPayment | Money paid to a supplier.
  - paid on : date !
  - amount : decimal !
  > pays > SupplierInvoice +
SupplierScorecard | A periodic rating of a supplier's performance.
  - period : string !
  - on time delivery percent : decimal
  - quality reject percent : decimal
  - overall score : decimal
  > rates > Supplier 1
rule: constraint | Three-way match | An invoice is paid only when its quantity and price agree with the purchase order and the goods receipt within tolerance. | SupplierInvoice, PurchaseOrder, GoodsReceipt
rule: constraint | Approved suppliers only | A purchase order can be placed only with a supplier whose status is Approved or Preferred. | PurchaseOrder, Supplier
rule: derivation | Maverick spend | Spend is maverick when a purchase order in a contracted category is not under a contract. | PurchaseOrder, Contract
rule: constraint | Approval first | A purchase order from a requisition requires the requisition to be Approved. | PurchaseOrder, Requisition
uc: Spend by category and supplier | Category manager | How much was spent per category and supplier this year, and how much of it under contract? | PurchaseOrder, PurchaseOrderLine, Item, SpendCategory, Supplier, Contract | has line, for item, Item.in category, placed with, under contract, PurchaseOrder.total value
uc: Late deliveries | Buyer | Which order lines were received after the promised date, by supplier? | PurchaseOrderLine, GoodsReceipt, PurchaseOrder, Supplier | against line, GoodsReceipt.received on, PurchaseOrderLine.promised date, PurchaseOrderLine.of order, placed with
uc: Invoices on hold | Accounts payable | Which invoices are held for a price or quantity variance? | SupplierInvoice, MatchStatus, Supplier | has match status, from supplier, SupplierInvoice.amount
